<title>FRANCE: Details of EU wheat-for-Africa target list.</title>
<headline>Details of EU wheat-for-Africa target list.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the list of countries which can receive European Union wheat sold with special subsidies for Africa, given by member-country officials.</p>
<p>Officials said earlier that up to a million tonnes of EU wheat was tentatively being sought for export to Africa by June 30 and another 150,000 tonnes for shorter expiry.</p>
<p>The list contains 38 mostly sub-Saharan states and has been stripped of those deemed U.S. markets like Nigeria. Traders said this was apparently meant to avoid more tension over subsidies.</p>
<p>    Mauritania			   Mali</p>
<p>    Niger				  Senegal</p>
<p>    Burkina Faso			 Gambia</p>
<p>    Guinea-Bissau			Guinea</p>
<p>    Cape Verde			   Sierra Leone</p>
<p>    Liberia				Ivory Coast</p>
<p>    Ghana				  Togo</p>
<p>    Chad				   Central African Republic</p>
<p>    Benin				  Cameroon</p>
<p>    Equatorial Guinea		  Sao Tome and Principe</p>
<p>    Gabon				  Congo</p>
<p>    Zaire				  Rwanda</p>
<p>    Burundi				Angola</p>
<p>    Zambia				 Malawi</p>
<p>    Mozambique			   Namibia</p>
<p>    Botswana			     Zimbabwe</p>
<p>    Lesotho				Swaziland</p>
<p>    Seychelles			   Comoros</p>
<p>    Madagascar			   Mauritius</p>
<p>Officials said the list of countries was expected to be published soon in the European Union's Official Journal.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
